I find (I'm now thoroughly spoiled, so this is with the benefit of that
extra knowledge) that most of the things that it's really helpful to
be spoiled about aren't the sort of thing you'll know to look for
spoilers on.

The "causes of instadeath in the late game" spoiler (that may not be its
real title), for example, contains lots of little spoilers from many
different aspects of the game, that would have been exactly the sort of
thing that I wouldn't have wanted to be spoiled on (before I started
reading any old spoilers).

The many different obscure object interactions, that can heavily tip the
balance in your favour if you know how to exploit them, are another
thing about which you would build up your knowledge *very* gradually,
often by guesswork or accident.  But you'd have to give up on playing
unspoiled and dive head-first into the spoiler sites in order to pick up
those helpful titbits.  (Or just read RGRN for months, and watch them all
crop up casually.)

